Z||000005||StuGood||01-25-2001||11:48 PM||||Thanks for all of the warm (but wet  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">) welcomes!  I'm sure it will be fun to live up there again, but moving is nearly always a little nerve-racking...  only about a week to go, and still so much to do - !<P>Last time, I had my silver GT up there in Everett, in 1990 I took my gold 1986 SE 4-speed and lived between Kent and Renton.    This time, it'll be the 1987 black Cav, since the Fieros are being worked on.  Talk about bad timing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Might have to see one of you guys, just to get my "Fiero fix!"   <P>Wonder if asking a realtor might be a good way to locate rental properties?  Usually, I have had very good luck scoping out the classifieds, etc., but haven't much time now.  Oh, well, Stu nearly always lucks out at the eleventh hour!  Why should this time be any different  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">? ||||reg||10
Z||000006||StuGood||03-23-2001||06:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by StuGood:<BR><B>Looks as though I'll be moving up to the  Everett, WA...  ...a few years ago, I lived in a townhome on Casino Road a little west of Evergreen Way...  ...I don't have a telephone number to call and inquire, though   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  - if anyone happens to have their number, please e-mail me... Thanks in advance  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Time to call off the search...<P>As usual, I lucked out at the eleventh hour again.  Didn't manage to get the old townhome, but <B>did</B> find:  Small house, double garage, reasonable rent [for Everett, anyway  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">] nice landlord, nice neighborhood, only two miles from work, and no freeway traffic to deal with!  Why do I even worry about these things  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ?<P>...Now all I have to worry about, is that they don't cancel the programs I'm working on, like they did in 1996!<P>Thanks to those of you who tried, or thought about trying, to help Stu out with this  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">     ||||reg||6
